---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Deflicker - François Pitié" currentSection="research">
  <div class="post">
    <header class="post-header mb-8">
      <div class="mb-2">
        <a href="/research" class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--theme-link)] hover:text-[var(--theme-accent)]">&larr; back to research</a>
      </div>
      <h1 class="post-title">Deflicker: Brightness & Exposure Stabilization</h1>
      <p class="desc text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1.5 pb-3 border-b border-[var(--theme-border)]">
        Statistical algorithms for localized flicker removal in archival film and high-speed video capture.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="space-y-10">
      <!-- Video Player Hero -->
      <div class="rounded overflow-hidden border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-black shadow-xs">
        <video 
          controls 
          loop 
          playsinline 
          class="w-full max-h-[480px] mx-auto bg-black"
        >
          <source src="/images/deflicker.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          Your browser does not support the video tag.
        </video>
        <div class="p-3 text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] border-t border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/70">
          <strong>Video Demo: </strong> Archival film before and after applying statistical localized deflicker processing.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Overview -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base text-[var(--theme-fg)] leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-light tracking-tight text-[var(--theme-heading)] pb-1.5 border-b border-[var(--theme-border)]">
          Overview
        </h2>
        <p>
          Brightness fluctuations, or <em>flicker</em>, are common in archival film (due to variable exposure and chemical aging) as well as high-speed video capture under oscillating artificial lighting.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because film degradation and non-uniform lighting rarely affect the entire frame uniformly, flicker is typically a spatially localized problem. We developed statistical estimators that combine motion-compensated temporal smoothing with localized gain and bias correction, stabilizing erratic brightness without affecting real scene motion or clipping highlights.
        </p>
        <p>
          This method was integrated into <strong>Furnace Deflicker2</strong> by The Foundry, where it has been widely used for archival film restoration.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Key Publications -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-light tracking-tight text-[var(--theme-heading)] pb-2 border-b border-[var(--theme-border)] mb-4">
          Key Publications
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/20">
            <div class="font-semibold text-sm text-[var(--theme-heading)] leading-snug">
              Localised Deflicker of Moving Images
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1">
              F. Pitié, B. Kent, B. Collis, and A. Kokaram
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-0.5 italic">
              3rd European Conference on Visual Media Production (CVMP), London, 2006.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-3.5 rounded border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/20">
            <div class="font-semibold text-sm text-[var(--theme-heading)] leading-snug">
              A New Robust Technique for Stabilizing Brightness Fluctuations
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1">
              F. Pitié, R. Dahyot, F. Kelly, and A. Kokaram
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-0.5 italic">
              2nd International Workshop on Statistical Methods in Video Processing (ECCV Workshop), Prague, 2004.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-3.5 rounded border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/20">
            <div class="font-semibold text-sm text-[var(--theme-heading)] leading-snug">
              Simultaneous Luminance and Position Stabilization for Film and Video
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1">
              A. Kokaram, R. Dahyot, F. Pitié, and H. Denman
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-0.5 italic">
              Visual Communications and Image Processing (VCIP), Lugano, 2003.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
